    faqs: [["What is the LMIA wage threshold in 2026?", "It depends on the province or territory and the date submitted. ESDC updates the information, so use the current official table rather than a single Canada-wide number."], ["Is prevailing wage the same as high-wage threshold?", "No. Prevailing wage assesses occupation and location, while the threshold selects the federal processing stream. The offered wage normally needs to satisfy both."], ["Can an employer pay below the Job Bank wage?", "The employer must follow the wage rules for the stream and occupation, including comparable-wage evidence and employment standards. A lower offer can create refusal or compliance risk."], ["Do wage rules affect permanent residence?", "The LMIA and permanent-residence processes are separate. A job supports a pathway only when the position, worker and program meet current criteria."], ["What should the employer save?", "Keep the job description, NOC comparison, location, wage source, comparable-worker information, recruitment evidence and payroll or budget records."]],
